## Robotstxt

The code chunk below will show the output from the [robotstxt package]

```{r robotxt}
robotstxt::paths_allowed(paths = "/courses-instruction/isa/", domain = "bulletin.miamioh.edu", bot = "*")

robotstxt::paths_allowed(paths = "/wiki/Miami_RedHawks_football", domain = "en.wikipedia.org", bot = "*")

robotstxt::paths_allowed(paths = "/jobs/", domain = "www.linkedin.com", bot = "*")

robotstxt::paths_allowed(paths = "/viewjob", domain = "www.indeed.com", bot = "*")


isa_page_in_r = rvest::read_html("https://bulletin.miamioh.edu/courses-instruction/isa/")

##extract the titles
## if all titels look the same on the page, it means that they have the smae tag/class which would allow yout to extract them in one step
## copy the selector
##highlighted the course
## right clicked the selecter inspect
## found the part that was flushed containtng the title
## right clicked and copied the selector
## saw the output from the code below just got  me the 24th course so I dropped the ':nth-child(24)


isa_page_in_r |> rvest::html_elements("#sc_sccoursedescs > div > p.courseblocktitle > strong") |>
  rvest::html_text2() -> isa_titles

isa_page_in_r |> 
  rvest::html_elements(".courseblockdesc") |> 
  rvest::html_text2() -> isa_descs

isa_df = data.frame(
  title = isa_titles, description = isa_descs
)


```
